{:edb/db-before-t 331 :edb/db-after-t 332 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533644 50 #inst "2026-10-04T05:54:08.286Z" 13194139533644 true] [17592186083136 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243685 13194139533644 true] [17592186083136 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243699 13194139533644 true] [17592186083136 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243748 13194139533644 true] [17592186083136 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243755 13194139533644 true] [17592186083136 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243762 13194139533644 true] [17592186083137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243692 13194139533644 true] [17592186083137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243727 13194139533644 true] [17592186083137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243769 13194139533644 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243678 13194139533644 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243706 13194139533644 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243720 13194139533644 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243741 13194139533644 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243790 13194139533644 true] [17592186083222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243713 13194139533644 true] [17592186083222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243734 13194139533644 true] [17592186083222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243776 13194139533644 true] [17592186083222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243783 13194139533644 true] [17592186083722 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533644 true] [17592186083722 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $10$ athletes, so $n=10.$ We want to select $3$ of those athletes to receive gold, silver, or bronze medals, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to award the medals is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{10}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{10!}{(10-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{7!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot \\cancel{7!}}{\\cancel{7!}} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =720.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533644 true] [17592186083724 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533644 true] [17592186083724 1145 "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=100$ and $r=0$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{100}{P}_{0} & =\\frac{100!}{(100-0)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{100!}}{\\cancel{100!}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533644 true] [17592186083730 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533644 true] [17592186083730 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $30$ shows to choose from, so $n=30.$ We want to select $4$ of those shows for the lineup, so we have $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different possible lineups is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{30}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{30!}{(30-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{30!}{26!} \\\\  & =\\frac{30\\cdot 29\\cdot 28\\cdot 27\\cdot \\cancel{26!}}{\\cancel{26!}} \\\\  & =30\\cdot 29\\cdot 28\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =657\\,720.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243678 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243679 13194139533644 true] [17592186243678 1089 "q-122218" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243678 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533644 true] [17592186243678 1100 "Evaluate $P(8,7).$" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243678 1113 #uuid "9432eaeb-dbd3-5904-ba90-006c3ed8458e" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243678 1138 false 13194139533644 true] [17592186243678 1145 "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(8,7)$ means the same thing as ${}_{8}{P}_{7}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8,7) & =\\frac{8!}{(8-7)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8!}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}{1} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40\\,320.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243680 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243681 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243682 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243683 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243684 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1041 "selection" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243682 13194139533644 true] [17592186243679 1110 #uuid "52c27f92-35e6-5027-8e45-3533e8acdf31" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243680 1034 "8" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243680 1111 #uuid "84db12e7-8a9b-5067-8eb1-8521432feef3" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243681 1034 "7" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243681 1111 #uuid "f72970e8-ae6d-5db8-85b9-86ca930bfda0" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243682 1034 "40\\,320" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243682 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243682 1111 #uuid "cc0d274b-650c-52c4-82e3-cc4f26489cca" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243683 1034 "20\\,160" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243683 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243683 1111 #uuid "20424e93-e1a4-57ac-aa86-b12e0da525f6" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243684 1034 "56\\,040" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243684 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243684 1111 #uuid "bae5ec16-eb64-5632-92d8-589f2fa42943" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243685 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243686 13194139533644 true] [17592186243685 1089 "q-122233" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243685 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533644 true] [17592186243685 1100 "Ashley has $5$ tasks. She decides to do one on Thursday and another on Friday. How many different choices of the two tasks does Ashley have?" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243685 1113 #uuid "8de5a14a-1960-5058-86a3-9b2c571140bb" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243685 1138 false 13194139533644 true] [17592186243685 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $5$ tasks to choose from, so $n=5.$ We want to select $2$ of those for Ashley to do, so we have $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{5}{P}_{2} & =\\frac{5!}{(5-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5!}{3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243687 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243688 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243689 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243690 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243691 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1041 "selection" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243687 13194139533644 true] [17592186243686 1110 #uuid "b000454b-8d8a-5922-aabd-1682d36a0d67" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243687 1034 "20" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243687 1111 #uuid "e0d4cc6c-817e-53a2-a366-c0d10cbe6a53" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243688 1034 "60" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243688 1111 #uuid "607fdaf5-7073-52b8-ae26-68adae34ab30" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243689 1034 "2" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243689 1111 #uuid "ec744e7f-bc4e-56b9-acfa-9c1ecac912f4" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243690 1034 "25" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243690 1111 #uuid "55f0e79f-797f-5833-9f14-c06a6304c31b" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243691 1034 "5" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533644 true] [17592186243691 1111 #uuid "4fab4e2f-7535-5870-b2a3-822e38827406" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243692 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243693 13194139533644 true] [17592186243692 1089 "q-122476" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243692 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533644 true] [17592186243692 1100 "How many $5$-letter words (legitimate or made-up) can be made using the letters of the word ALGORITHMS, where each letter cannot appear in the word more than once?" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243692 1113 #uuid "8f3b348f-3d24-534c-8714-77102243eca3" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243692 1138 false 13194139533644 true] [17592186243692 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $10$ different letters in the word ALGORITHMS, so $n=10.$ We want to select $5$ of those letters to make a $5$-letter word, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different made-up words is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{10}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{10!}{(10-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30\\,240.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243694 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243695 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243696 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243697 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243698 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1041 "selection" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243697 13194139533644 true] [17592186243693 1110 #uuid "94e036ff-6e89-5e29-b08a-5f577562cbcd" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243694 1034 "151\\,200" 13194139533644 true] [17592186243694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194